# Auto-commit

After a code change is finished and checks that apply have been run, commit it and push to the tracked remote before ending the turn.

- Commit only the files changed for that task.
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, tokens).
- Push the current branch after the commit. Do not force-push.
- Do not commit when the worktree has no changes.
- Use a short message that says why the change was made.
